1
00:01:31,830 --> 00:01:35,920
EPISODE 4: ALLEN SPILLS THE BEANS

2
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:35,580
How can I get out of this? Gotta think fast!

3
00:01:39,830 --> 00:01:41,250
Help me out, Sucker!

4
00:01:47,170 --> 00:01:49,330
Awesome! That did some damage!

5
00:01:49,750 --> 00:01:54,130
I never tested it to be sure, but I was right
about these guys having an energy drain attack!

6
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:59,330
I'm weaker after losing so many
of my summons and their buffs,

7
00:01:59,330 --> 00:02:02,040
but that's not a problem
if I can just cripple this thing instead!

8
00:02:02,130 --> 00:02:03,170
Fido! Sucker!

9
00:02:19,750 --> 00:02:23,130
YOU HAVE DEFEATED 1 ALBAHERON.

10
00:02:19,750 --> 00:02:23,130
YOU HAVE GAINED 100 EXP.

11
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:22,920
Oh, man...

12
00:02:23,210 --> 00:02:26,330
I WOOOOON!

13
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:30,210
I beat my first monster!

14
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:33,460
This is giving me a rush beyond words!

15
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:36,420
An albaheron?!

16
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:37,960
Look what I got!

17
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:39,750
How did you manage that?!

18
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:43,250
It happened to land nearby,
so I took it by surprise!

19
00:02:43,420 --> 00:02:45,330
That's mostly true.

20
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:47,880
You're amazing, Allen!

21
00:02:48,250 --> 00:02:49,630
It's scawy!

22
00:02:49,630 --> 00:02:52,580
Don't worry, Mash. It won't move or anything.

23
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:57,130
Hey. You've got a cut on your cheek.
Are you hurt anywhere else?

24
00:02:57,210 --> 00:02:59,330
The bleeding stopped already. I'm fine!

25
00:02:59,710 --> 00:03:04,290
This is real impressive, kid. You took it down
with your wooden sword and some rocks?

26
00:03:04,290 --> 00:03:04,920
Yep!

27
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:07,960
Uh, I see some dog-like bite marks here.

28
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:08,630
Huh?!

29
00:03:08,630 --> 00:03:09,880
Did you bite it, Allen?

30
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:10,960
Oh crap!

31
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:14,420
I-I'm not sure, I was fighting on pure instinct...

32
00:03:14,670 --> 00:03:17,000
Chomp! Chomp! Chomp! Chomp! Chomp! Chomp!

33
00:03:14,670 --> 00:03:17,000
Ow! Ow! Ow!

34
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:20,920
Oh, right.

35
00:03:21,330 --> 00:03:23,670
Rodin. I'll bleed it out for ya.

36
00:03:23,670 --> 00:03:25,380
Thanks. Please do.

37
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:29,290
Wow! That's one big lump.

38
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:33,290
Bet he got that while playing knights with Krena.

39
00:03:33,290 --> 00:03:35,630
Gerda must be slow on his feet.

40
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:38,290
Hey, Allen.

41
00:03:38,710 --> 00:03:40,000
Lend me a hand.

42
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:44,170
Albaherons weigh 60 kilos on average.

43
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:47,630
That drops to 20 kilos after you
drain the blood and dry 'em out.

44
00:03:47,830 --> 00:03:49,880
Only half of that is edible meat, though.

45
00:03:50,290 --> 00:03:51,920
Their wings fetch a pretty penny, too.

46
00:03:52,330 --> 00:03:55,250
I'm happy he's willing to teach me all this!

47
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:59,130
Though, we still gotta fork over
most of it to the upper class.

48
00:03:59,290 --> 00:04:04,250
Huh? The sixty percent tax
even applies to wild monsters?

49
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:05,040
Yep.

50
00:04:05,170 --> 00:04:08,380
They're nice enough to overlook
smaller ones like E-rank horned rabbits.

51
00:04:08,630 --> 00:04:11,080
But albaherons are D-rank.

52
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:13,210
What a bum deal.

53
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:14,580
One more thing.

54
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:17,540
Almost... got it!

55
00:04:18,330 --> 00:04:19,500
This is a magic stone.

56
00:04:19,790 --> 00:04:20,960
Oh yeah?

57
00:04:21,290 --> 00:04:24,540
Magic stones from any monster
above D-rank fall under the tax.

58
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:27,750
No biggie, though.
They're worthless to us in the village anyways.

59
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,170
But listen!

60
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:36,880
A kid like you wouldn't be out there catching
monsters if your dad hadn't gotten hurt so bad.

61
00:04:37,210 --> 00:04:40,380
We can use that as leverage
to negotiate a bigger cut with the chieftain.

62
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:41,710
Oh, I see.

63
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:44,000
I think I have an idea, Mister Gerda!

64
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:47,880
Whisper, whisper, whisper.

65
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:51,830
CHIEFTAIN'S RESIDENCE

66
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:51,830
So, there you have it.

67
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:56,420
Rodin's youngster stuck his little neck out
to nab this monster.

68
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:58,420
Ah, I see! Wonderful!

69
00:04:58,670 --> 00:04:59,580
Here's the deal.

70
00:04:59,580 --> 00:05:00,210
Huh?

71
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:02,830
We'll fork over the entirety of its wings as tax.

72
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,250
But you don't mind us taking the rest, yeah?

73
00:05:05,420 --> 00:05:08,040
Ah, I see. Wonder-fuh?

74
00:05:08,130 --> 00:05:10,040
C'mon. That's not such a big deal, is it?

75
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:11,540
Wait, wait, wait!

76
00:05:11,670 --> 00:05:13,420
That's a problem!

77
00:05:13,540 --> 00:05:17,880
The baron has asked that we deliver
even more meat this year, you see.

78
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:20,040
You understand what that means, right?

79
00:05:20,250 --> 00:05:21,880
Huh? The baron did?

80
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:25,330
Is that why the chief was so insistent
on having commoners join the hunt?

81
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:27,040
You drive a hard bargain.

82
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:29,460
Fine, we'll throw in
the magic stone, too. How's that?

83
00:05:29,670 --> 00:05:32,210
Huh? Just the wings and the magic stone?

84
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:37,000
Well, shucks! If only SOMEBODY
hadn't asked the impossible of us.

85
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:39,960
Then maybe our resident hero, Rodin,
wouldn't have gotten hurt so badly.

86
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:42,670
Now his poor family is on the verge
of starving to death.

87
00:05:42,670 --> 00:05:45,000
How can they survive the winter
with four mouths to feed?

88
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,670
Oh! I'm so hungry!

89
00:05:48,630 --> 00:05:49,460
It's making me dizzy...

90
00:05:49,460 --> 00:05:52,130
Oh no, Allen! Hang in there!

91
00:05:52,130 --> 00:05:55,960
Heavens me! Just WHO can we blame
for this awful predicament?

92
00:05:56,130 --> 00:05:58,540
Aw, all right! I get it!

93
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:02,920
I do owe a lot to Rodin for his work.
I suppose you can have it.

94
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:07,880
Boom, baby! That's how we do it!

95
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:10,130
Thank you, chief!

96
00:06:11,330 --> 00:06:12,540
Don't mention it...

97
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:19,500
So, in the future, we can keep the meat and just
give you the wings and magic stones, right?

98
00:06:19,710 --> 00:06:20,290
Huh?!

99
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:23,130
This is the real crux of the issue!

100
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:25,080
Come now, Allen!

101
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:28,790
It's not good to count your albaherons
before they've hatched!

102
00:06:28,790 --> 00:06:32,460
They're tough to get. Right, chief?

103
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:35,000
Way to sell him on it!

104
00:06:35,170 --> 00:06:37,420
That's a good point.

105
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:42,000
I suppose you can keep the meat if you're
lucky enough to wrangle another one. Do your best.

106
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:42,830
It's a done deal!

107
00:06:43,250 --> 00:06:49,130
Ribbit. Ribbit. Ribbit. Ribbit. Ribbit. Ribbit.

108
00:06:50,830 --> 00:06:52,830
Whoa! Two of them?!

109
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:55,000
Hopper! That's enough!

110
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,040
Ribbit. Ribbit. Ribbit.

111
00:06:59,830 --> 00:07:00,670
Suck 'em dry!

112
00:07:09,790 --> 00:07:11,080
Take this!

113
00:07:13,670 --> 00:07:15,040
Give 'em the fangs, Fido!

114
00:07:18,330 --> 00:07:19,380
Knock 'em down!

115
00:07:27,710 --> 00:07:29,080
And make it double!

116
00:07:31,170 --> 00:07:34,540
Woot! Now that's what I call a two for one!

117
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:36,580
Okay, everybody! Return!

118
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:42,380
I've been out hunting once every three days
since beating that first one,

119
00:07:42,630 --> 00:07:44,830
but this is the first time
I didn't lose any summons!

120
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,580
Flawless victory, baby!

121
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:52,540
YOU HAVE DEFEATED

122
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:52,540
2 ALBAHERONS.

123
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:52,540
YOU HAVE GAINED 200 EXP.

124
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,170
Sweet.

125
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:55,920
YOUR EXP HAS REACHED

126
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:55,920
THE MAX OF 1000/1000.

127
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:55,580
Huh?

128
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:59,630
YOU HAVE GONE UP

129
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:59,630
TO LEVEL 2.

