Alright! Those are big gains!

191
00:08:31,540 --> 00:08:32,250
Bring it in.

192
00:08:33,750 --> 00:08:35,710
Six years after being reincarnated.

193
00:08:35,710 --> 00:08:37,920
I've finally hit my first level up.

194
00:08:38,330 --> 00:08:41,920
So this is what it's like to pass
a "Trial of the Gods", huh?

195
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:43,290
Feels amazing.

196
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:47,380
It might be time that I
let the fam in on the truth.

197
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:52,210
I'm home!

198
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:53,670
Oh, welcome back.

199
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:56,960
Whoa! You caught two of them today?!

200
00:08:56,960 --> 00:09:00,500
Yep! I actually beat them at the same time.
Pretty amazing, huh?

201
00:09:00,750 --> 00:09:02,540
Huh? Wait a sec, Allen...

202
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:03,250
What is it?

203
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:06,790
Never mind. It's nothing.

204
00:09:08,210 --> 00:09:09,750
Ah! I gotta go!

205
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:17,000
With today's hunt,
I've met my goal of 10 monsters.

206
00:09:17,460 --> 00:09:20,250
Once I dry the meat,
we'll have enough to make it through winter!

207
00:09:22,210 --> 00:09:24,130
The only thing left now is to trade for firewood!

208
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:29,460
Since there are a lot of albaherons around
for migration season,

209
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:31,670
I could try to hit level three by hunting 20 more.

210
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,960
But that'll be hard to do
before the end of the year.

211
00:09:35,170 --> 00:09:35,880
Huh?

212
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:37,540
Ow!

213
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:40,420
See ya tomorrow!

214
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:49,380
So, you wanted to talk with us?

215
00:09:50,170 --> 00:09:53,170
Yeah. This might throw you for a loop, but...

216
00:09:53,670 --> 00:09:58,170
to tell the truth, I heard an oracle from God
back when I was one year old.

217
00:09:58,460 --> 00:09:59,500
An oracle?

218
00:09:59,790 --> 00:10:01,500
Are you talking about Lord Elmea?

219
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:02,920
That's right.

220
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:08,500
"Young Allen. I shall bless you
with power and wisdom."

221
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:09,500
So he said!

222
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:13,210
What is that supposed to mean, exactly?

223
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:18,540
It basically means I'm smarter
and physically stronger than your average person.

224
00:10:18,790 --> 00:10:20,290
But at the same time...

225
00:10:20,540 --> 00:10:25,040
"You shall be faced with trials beyond
what even a hundred men could accomplish."

226
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:28,880
"Use your blessings of power
and wisdom to overcome them."

227
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:29,880
So, yeah!

228
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:31,380
A hundred men?!

229
00:10:31,790 --> 00:10:34,630
Oh, Lord! How could you do this to my Allen?!

230
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:40,040
I see. You must have bested
one of those trials today, huh?

231
00:10:40,540 --> 00:10:44,960
You probably haven't noticed, but the cut you had
on your cheek this morning has disappeared.

232
00:10:45,170 --> 00:10:47,500
Huh? Oh...

233
00:10:48,170 --> 00:10:50,290
I know what it's like to pass a Trial of the Gods.

234
00:10:50,540 --> 00:10:52,210
I figured that's what happened with you.

235
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:53,710
Oh yeah?

236
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:57,000
Wait, but what about your results
from last year's Appraisal Ceremony?

237
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,290
I got another oracle from Elmea
about that a couple months ago.

238
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:04,210
Jeez, that recently?!
But wait a minute, show proper respect!

239
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:06,000
That's LORD Elmea to you, got it?

240
00:11:06,130 --> 00:11:09,540
Sure, I'll be careful from now on.

241
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:10,420
Good.

242
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:13,710
The reason my attributes were ranked so low
at the Appraisal Ceremony

243
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:17,330
is because they take the slower progression
of my trials into account.

244
00:11:17,670 --> 00:11:19,380
And the reason I was judged not to have a talent

245
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:22,500
is because mine was actually
too new to be recognized.

246
00:11:22,630 --> 00:11:25,630
Wait, so you DO have a talent?

247
00:11:25,630 --> 00:11:26,710
What kind is it?

248
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,420
Well, he never told me what it was...

249
00:11:29,670 --> 00:11:31,130
Shoot.

250
00:11:32,250 --> 00:11:36,130
Sorry, Dad. I can't say anything
about being a Summoner yet.

251
00:11:36,710 --> 00:11:39,130
I'm worried some people
might get the wrong idea

252
00:11:39,130 --> 00:11:41,630
if they find out I can summon
and control creatures.

253
00:11:42,130 --> 00:11:44,290
And naturally, I can't tell anybody
that I was reincarnated.

254
00:11:46,500 --> 00:11:49,500
Oh, Allen! I wish you would have told us sooner!

255
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:53,460
Your habit of throwing
those rocks at trees every day,

256
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:56,290
and now hunting these big monsters,

257
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:59,080
it's because you've been fighting
to overcome the Lord's trial, huh?

258
00:11:59,250 --> 00:12:00,500
And all by yourself!

259
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:02,420
I'm sorry, Mom.

260
00:12:04,790 --> 00:12:05,960
You little dummy.

261
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:08,960
So, what are you going to do now?

262
00:12:09,250 --> 00:12:09,960
Well...

263
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:13,040
I want to prove myself worthy
by passing the trials.

264
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:15,420
So I'll be brave and take them head-on.

265
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:18,330
All right. I figured as much.

266
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:22,420
Lord Elmea prepared this challenge
specifically for you.

267
00:12:23,250 --> 00:12:24,710
It's worth taking up the gauntlet.

268
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:28,670
And if you run into trouble,
don't hesitate to ask for our help.

269
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:29,880
Okay.

270
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:33,290
Thanks so much! Dad, Mom!

271
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:37,330
Hey, Allen? Keep this all between us for now.

272
00:12:37,580 --> 00:12:40,290
It would be bad if anyone took you
for a false prophet.

273
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:43,540
But... do you mind if I tell Gerda?

274
00:12:43,630 --> 00:12:45,670
Huh? Sure, that's fine with me.

275
00:12:45,670 --> 00:12:47,210
Okay, great!

276
00:12:47,330 --> 00:12:50,290
He's always bragging about
how Krena's a Sword Lord and all.

277
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:53,420
Now I can tell him that my son
is just as incredible!

278
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:58,960
THE HARDCORE GAMER DOMINATES

279
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:58,960
IN ANOTHER WORLD WITH GARBAGE BALANCING

280
00:12:59,540 --> 00:13:01,920
ALLEN - AGE 6

281
00:13:11,380 --> 00:13:14,420
Well, I always figured you were no ordinary kid.

282
00:13:14,750 --> 00:13:17,380
But getting blessed and tested
by God is something else.

283
00:13:20,290 --> 00:13:23,790
It explains a lot, though.
Rodin must be beside himself.

284
00:13:26,210 --> 00:13:28,040
This is your first time
trading for supplies, yeah?

285
00:13:28,170 --> 00:13:30,460
Yes. Please show me the ropes.

286
00:13:30,750 --> 00:13:33,380
Good thing you stocked up on those albaheron, eh?

287
00:13:33,750 --> 00:13:35,630
Seems like your boar hunt was fruitful, too!

288
00:13:35,750 --> 00:13:40,290
Things go smoothly when it's just us serfs
and no commoners to muck it up!

289
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:44,500
What's the real difference
between serfs and commoners, anyway?

290
00:13:44,750 --> 00:13:47,540
Well, our social standing, for one.

291
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:52,920
Also our taxes. The sixty percent rule
doesn't apply to commoners.

292
00:13:53,170 --> 00:13:55,040
They have what's called a "head tax" instead.

293
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:59,250
They pay three gold coins for each adult
and one for each kid every year.

294
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:01,210
Oh, that's interesting.

295
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:03,080
And now, I slip in my real question...

296
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:06,040
Is there any way for serfs to become commoners?

297
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:10,130
There is. You gotta make a tribute
of 10 gold coins per person in the family.

298
00:14:10,670 --> 00:14:14,880
I've also heard stories that the baron
can reward people with commoner status,

299
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:16,290
but I dunno if that's true or not.

300
00:14:16,420 --> 00:14:18,250
I see.

301
00:14:18,750 --> 00:14:23,380
My family's about to get a new member.
So it would cost us 50 gold coins, huh?

302
00:14:30,170 --> 00:14:31,830
I'm trading in five packs of boar jerky.

303
00:14:38,670 --> 00:14:39,960
Okay, I'll do the same.

304
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:42,920
I'd like to trade in five packs
of albaheron jerky.

305
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:49,080
Awesome!

306
00:14:54,420 --> 00:14:55,290
Here ya go.

307
00:14:59,210 --> 00:15:00,040
Whoa!

308
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:05,500
One pack of jerky trades
for four days worth of firewood.

309
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:08,130
Now that I know how bartering works,

310
00:15:08,290 --> 00:15:10,500
I can do a bit of market research
next time I'm here.

311
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:20,380
Thank you, sir.

312
00:15:20,380 --> 00:15:22,920
May I ask how much
this would cost to buy with money?

313
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:24,380
Five silver coins.

314
00:15:24,580 --> 00:15:25,420
Thanks.

315
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,670
Can't be a salt merchant without
a "salty" attitude, I guess.

316
00:15:29,540 --> 00:15:32,170
What is that fruit hanging down over there?

317
00:15:32,170 --> 00:15:33,830
We call those "popos".

318
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,040
They trade one-for-one with a bundle of your meat.

319
00:15:37,210 --> 00:15:39,630
Jeez, expensive! That's four times
the rate for molmos.

320
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:41,250
You want one of those instead?

321
00:15:41,250 --> 00:15:42,960
No, sir! I'll keep these.

322
00:15:46,750 --> 00:15:50,290
A single bundle of albaheron jerky trades for:

323
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:51,830
One bag of salt.

324
00:15:51,830 --> 00:15:53,170
Four molmo fruits.

325
00:15:53,170 --> 00:15:54,460
One popo fruit.

326
00:15:54,460 --> 00:15:55,920
Four days worth of firewood.

327
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,330
The following forms of currency
have the same value:

328
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:00,920
One gold coin. A hundred silver coins.

329
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:03,540
A thousand copper coins. Ten thousand iron coins.

330
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:06,580
One bundle of jerky goes for one silver coin.

331
00:16:06,710 --> 00:16:09,040
So saving up for 50 gold coins would mean...

332
00:16:09,170 --> 00:16:11,460
hunting 500 albaherons.

333
00:16:11,750 --> 00:16:14,000
Nice. That would only take a few years!

334
00:16:14,210 --> 00:16:16,330
A walk in the park for a hardcore gamer like me!

335
00:16:17,250 --> 00:16:18,420
Pardon me!

336
00:16:19,380 --> 00:16:21,750
Do you have any medicines that recover MP?

337
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:22,920
Huh?

338
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:25,750
We don't carry anything that fancy 'round here.

339
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:27,380
Oh, really?

340
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:29,000
Where are the healing medicines?

341
00:16:29,130 --> 00:16:30,580
Towards the back.

342
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:36,380
I wonder if my notebook can make drawings, too?

343
00:16:39,210 --> 00:16:40,960
Oh! It worked!

344
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:43,880
It pays to try things out. Which reminds me...

345
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:47,500
Excuse me, which of these is the muellerze flower?

346
00:16:48,170 --> 00:16:51,790
I don't have any of those!
And even if I did, I won't cut any deals for it!

347
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:53,790
Oh, I'm sorry.

348
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:58,170
Yeesh. I'm still frustrated
over the last one I sold.

349
00:16:58,380 --> 00:17:01,960
Do you mean the one Mister Gerda
bought about a month ago?

350
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:04,330
Yeah, exactly! That darn Gerda fellow!

351
00:17:04,330 --> 00:17:09,290
He burst in here all of a sudden and demanded
my best medicine. He was beyond insistent!

352
00:17:09,630 --> 00:17:11,580
And so, you sold him a muellerze flower?

353
00:17:11,710 --> 00:17:14,250
Well, I happened to have one in stock that day.

354
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:16,210
But when I told him it cost five gold coins,

355
00:17:16,210 --> 00:17:18,500
he begged me to settle
for three and promised to pay later.

356
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:21,830
He kept hollering about some friend needing help.
He even dropped to his hands and knees!

357
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,250
Gerda's a real bro...

358
00:17:23,750 --> 00:17:28,880
Anyways, the guy was more persistent than a kid
at a candy store. I had to let him have it.

359
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:31,830
But I was biting my nails like crazy
until he brought the money.

360
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:34,210
Still, it was a bad deal. I lost out in the end.

361
00:17:34,210 --> 00:17:35,540
It really irks me!

362
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,670
Here. For you.

363
00:17:40,080 --> 00:17:42,750
Oh, sorry for going off like that!
You're here to trade, right?

364
00:17:42,750 --> 00:17:44,830
What would you like? Just let me know.

365
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:47,380
No. I'm giving this to you.

366
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:49,170
Huh? What for?

367
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:54,880
You did a great service selling that muellerze
flower at a discount. It saved my father's life.

368
00:17:54,880 --> 00:17:55,540
Oh my...

369
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:58,750
This is a token of my appreciation.
I'll bring more next time!

370
00:17:59,330 --> 00:18:00,710
Thank you, sir.

371
00:18:00,710 --> 00:18:02,210
Aw, don't mention it.

372
00:18:06,170 --> 00:18:10,040
Holy crap! Just one of those
costs 50 silver coins?!

373
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:11,710
That's five albaherons...

374
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:14,250
Hey!

375
00:18:15,130 --> 00:18:17,790
Whatchu want with my family's shop, dirthead?

376
00:18:17,790 --> 00:18:21,790
This joker again.
Guess his dad is a blacksmith, huh?

377
00:18:22,080 --> 00:18:24,040
That's the chieftain's son hanging out with him.

378
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:26,880
Nothing in particular. Bye.

379
00:18:28,250 --> 00:18:29,210
Take this!

380
00:18:29,750 --> 00:18:30,960
What was that for?!

381
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:33,500
You only get to pass if you agree to be my minion!

382
00:18:34,670 --> 00:18:36,880
Who does he think he is,
a player killer in an MMO?

383
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:40,790
PVP doesn't score any EXP,
so I usually never bother with it.

384
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:46,960
What's wrong? You chicken out already?

385
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:49,040
Th-that's not fair!

386
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:51,290
You think that excuse will work
on the battlefield?

387
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:53,000
Mister tough guy.

388
00:18:54,790 --> 00:18:58,790
Go grab whatever weapon you want.
I'll wait right here.

389
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:02,130
Fine! You better not run, punk!

390
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:04,170
Keep an eye on him, Pelmoas!

391
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:07,790
Hi there, Pelmoas.

392
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:10,080
Uh, hey, Allen.

393
00:19:12,170 --> 00:19:13,750
I'll give you some credit!

394
00:19:13,750 --> 00:19:15,420
You had the balls to stick around!

395
00:19:16,330 --> 00:19:17,920
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

396
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:19,210
Cheap move!

397
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:27,710
His attacks hit pretty hard.
Makes sense for an Axe User.

398
00:19:28,130 --> 00:19:31,000
But he hardly compares
to the three-star power of Krena.

399
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:34,790
What's the big idea? Come at me, already!

400
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:45,960
Dogora, Knight of the Axe.

401
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:49,170
I'll be back to trade at your store someday.

402
00:19:52,330 --> 00:19:53,250
See ya.

403
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,710
Dammit!

404
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:08,290
Feast your eyes. I'm back in tip-top shape!

405
00:20:08,830 --> 00:20:11,250
Just don't pull a muscle by overexerting yourself.

406
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:12,460
Right!

407
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:16,380
AT KRENA'S HOUSE

408
00:20:18,380 --> 00:20:19,250
Ow!

409
00:20:19,420 --> 00:20:23,210
When will you learn, Dogora?
I told you to anticipate my moves.

410
00:20:23,210 --> 00:20:24,670
Yeah, I know!

411
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:28,040
Why can't I land a hit, dammit?!

412
00:20:30,420 --> 00:20:31,210
Hiyah!

413
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:36,420
I can tell Krena's taking it super easy on him.

414
00:20:36,830 --> 00:20:39,290
But Mash is doing pretty good, actually.

415
00:20:39,290 --> 00:20:41,500
He might have the talent of a Spear User!

416
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:43,250
You're wide open!

417
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:44,710
Ouch!

418
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:48,170
Big brudder! I like this thing!

419
00:20:48,290 --> 00:20:50,380
Oh yeah? That's great!

420
00:20:50,630 --> 00:20:53,080
I'm excited to see how
your Appraisal Ceremony will go in two years!

421
00:20:53,380 --> 00:20:55,830
Dammit! I'm not done yet!

422
00:21:02,420 --> 00:21:04,750
Wow, Myulla is so cute!

423
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:08,000
There was a time you were this cute, too.

424
00:21:08,380 --> 00:21:10,710
My own little prince charming.

425
00:21:10,920 --> 00:21:12,040
Shucks...

426
00:21:13,290 --> 00:21:14,130
I'm back.

427
00:21:14,420 --> 00:21:15,750
Welcome home!

428
00:21:16,790 --> 00:21:18,210
You're later than usual.

429
00:21:18,880 --> 00:21:20,290
And Mister Gerda's with you?

430
00:21:21,040 --> 00:21:22,920
We were summoned by the chieftain.

431
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:27,040
Here's the deal.

432
00:21:27,460 --> 00:21:33,330
The cheftain wants us to raise the number of boars
that we deliver to the baron from 10 to 15.

433
00:21:34,630 --> 00:21:38,830
And to make that happen, he expects us to let
the commoners join the hunt again this year.

434
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:42,210
Ridiculous! After you suffered that awful injury?!

435
00:21:42,380 --> 00:21:44,040
We wanted to say no, of course.

436
00:21:44,540 --> 00:21:47,330
But this order came directly
from the baron, apparently.

437
00:21:47,750 --> 00:21:50,420
If we don't deliver 15 boars by winter this year,

438
00:21:50,420 --> 00:21:52,920
they're going to recruit
more serfs from elsewhere.

439
00:21:53,540 --> 00:21:58,330
More serfs in the village
results in less land to go around.

440
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:03,290
Which means that serfs who can't hunt
might have their land taken away from them.

441
00:22:03,580 --> 00:22:07,670
And that risks changing
the very nature of Krena Village.

442
00:22:08,420 --> 00:22:11,170
Worse yet, they want us
to hunt 20 boars next year.

443
00:22:11,170 --> 00:22:13,380
No way! That's impossible!

444
00:22:13,630 --> 00:22:18,000
The only way to make it happen is for us to hunt
more often than the usual once every ten days.

445
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:21,210
But that just means greater risks
for everyone involved!

446
00:22:21,290 --> 00:22:25,040
The opinions of a few serfs can't compete
with the orders of the baron.

447
00:22:25,500 --> 00:22:27,000
No matter how unfair it seems.

448
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:28,000
This is awful!

449
00:22:28,580 --> 00:22:31,330
Yeah, it's not fair. But...

450
00:22:31,830 --> 00:22:33,540
We don't have the luxury of choice.

451
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:36,130
Okay, let's say that you
increase the number of hunts.

452
00:22:37,040 --> 00:22:41,830
Then they'll just keep expecting more from you
over the years, until it soon becomes impossible.

453
00:22:42,040 --> 00:22:44,670
The ultimate result is still
recruiting more serfs, right?

454
00:22:44,830 --> 00:22:47,170
Hey, Allen. Don't interupt when the adults are-

455
00:22:48,250 --> 00:22:50,210
Yeah. You make a good point.

456
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:54,710
Are you suggesting we do what the chieftain says
and let commoners join the hunt again?

457
00:22:55,130 --> 00:22:56,210
Pretty much.

458
00:22:56,210 --> 00:22:56,830
Out of the question!

459
00:22:56,960 --> 00:22:59,250
Those fools are nothing but dead weight!

460
00:22:59,330 --> 00:23:01,250
Then you have to find a way to make them useful.

461
00:23:02,500 --> 00:23:06,710
Listen. I have wisdom
that was blessed to me by Lord Elmea.

462
00:23:07,330 --> 00:23:09,580
I've spent countless hours across numerous games,

463
00:23:09,750 --> 00:23:12,630
making characters as strong
as they could possibly be.

464
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:14,630
Both flying solo and in pairs.

465
00:23:14,790 --> 00:23:18,960
I know how to integrate a newbie into a party
so they can safely gain the necessary EXP.

466
00:23:19,830 --> 00:23:22,670
Will you let me handle all this?

467
00:23:23,460 --> 00:23:25,250
I think I know how to make it work.

